# Sketch format

The source of truth is `skills/process-to-sketch/format_specification.md`, section 8. Start every sketch from `skills/process-to-sketch/sketch-template.md`.

## Location

- Every new sketch lives in its own new project directory, created by `python3 scripts/new_project.py "<Title>"`: `projects/<slug>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/<slug>.md`.
- The JSON `id` is that directory name.
- Never write a new sketch into an existing project directory, and never overwrite another project's files.

## Order of sections

`# Title` → the "Sketched in Architecture Viewer on <date>. All data is synthesized for the exercise." line → `## Technical discovery` → `## Pains` → `## As-is process` + `### As-is steps` → `## Proposed architecture` + `### Proposed steps` → `## Pain scorecard` → optional `## Implementation notes` → the JSON comment, last.

## Keys

- As-is keys are `Ⓐ Ⓑ Ⓒ …` and proposed keys `① ② ③ …`, in row order, in the first column of each step table.
- Every box label starts with the keys of the steps linked to it: `INTAKE["① ② Intake<br/>asks once"]`.
- A step without a box is listed in a comment: `%% Steps without a box yet: Ⓑ`.
- An arrow linked to a step that doesn't run between two of its boxes gets a `%% @step ④: FROM-->TO` line.
- The last line of each diagram is `%% @exact` with all its keys.

## Labels and ids

- Quote every label. Use `<br/>` for line breaks. The first line is the name.
- Escape `<` and `>` in labels as `&lt;` and `&gt;`.
- Mermaid ids are the label in capitals, with `_` for spaces and punctuation, at most 24 characters, unique. Never use `end`, `graph` or `subgraph` as an id.
- As-is boxes with pains end with a line `⚠ P1 P3`. Proposed boxes never carry `⚠` tags.
- Pain cells: `⚠ P1 <text>` in the as-is table, `P1 <text>` in the proposed table, several separated by `, `.

## Groups

- Every top-level `subgraph` has a `%% @overview <ID>: <title> | <role>` line.
- A human gate's label starts with `🔒`.

## JSON

- Header line exactly `<!-- architecture-viewer-sketch`, the JSON on the next lines, `-->` on its own line.
- `"v":3`, a stable `id` (a slug of the title), `dir` set to `"LR"` or `"TD"` on both boards.
- Never write `--` inside the JSON comment. Write `-\u002d` instead.
- Node labels in the JSON carry no step keys and no `⚠` tags.
- The JSON and the Markdown describe the same groups, boxes, arrows, steps and pains.

## Check

- Run `python3 scripts/check_sketch.py projects/<id>/<slug>.md` after every write, and fix every error before you report back.
